  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Engagement of Civil Society Organizations on Kenya&apos;s National Climate Plan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is a learning project with a key aim to understand how the Nationally Determined Contributions are at the heart of the Paris Agreement and the achievement of its long -term goals. NDCs embody efforts by each country to reduce national emissions and adapt to the impacts of climate change. It is therefore important to understand how inclusive NDC processes have been in Kenya and determine whether the quality of national climate responses can be improved through empowering understanding and engagement in NDCs by civil society, and by women, youth and indigenous peoples. The primary audience for this research is Oxfam as well as civil society, including partners of Oxfam, governments updating or implementing their NDCs, experts who are assisting governments with their NDC, donors who are providing climate finance to support conditional financial needs expressed in NDCs, policy makers and influencers.  The research will involve a mixed methods approach through an external consultant via a literature review and Key informant interviews at national &amp; county level (Turkana, Kwale &amp; Nairobi). The study will be carried out between June and July 2023 and a sense making workshop in August 2023.</narrative>
  </description>
